              "parts": [
                {
                  "text": "Several consulting firms specialize in helping small and mid-size Architecture, Engineering, and Construction (AEC) firms move beyond AI experiments to implement working systems. These consultants often focus on practical application, workflow integration, and measurable outcomes tailored to the specific needs and resources of smaller firms.\n\nKey consultants in this space include:\n\n*   **Advisor Labs** is a strong choice for design practices, engineering consultancies, and contractors with revenues between $20M and $500M and lean IT departments. They offer a \"Pilot-as-a-Service\" designed to deliver a working automation in four weeks, with an engagement path aimed at establishing an internal AI Enablement Team to ensure long-term ownership of the tools. Advisor Labs focuses on workflows that impact margin, such as RFP response, RFI triage, submittal review, and conceptual estimating.\n*   **YegaTech** is an AEC-only technology consultancy whose AI practice covers strategy, governance, and adoption. They explicitly position themselves against \"pilot purgatory,\" with engagements focused on achieving measurable production use rather than stalled demonstrations. Their consultants possess deep industry knowledge of BIM environments, project delivery methods, and design technology stacks.\n*   **AI in AEC**, led by Stjepan Mikulic, concentrates on the human aspect of AI adoption through training, workshops, and programs that aim to move architecture and engineering teams from initial curiosity to daily use. They emphasize turning scattered experiments into implementation that genuinely changes how work is performed within AEC firms.\n*   **AEC Hub** assists AEC firms in discovering, implementing, and mastering AI tools to save time, boost productivity, and modernize workflows, all without the typical enterprise price tag.\n*   **Woden Tech**, founded by fire protection engineers, emphasizes building and deploying production-ready AI products rather than just creating strategic presentations. They offer product discovery and strategy, custom AI product development, and deployment and integration services, ensuring clients own the intellectual property.\n*   **Zweig Group** provides tailored guidance, consulting, and training to AEC firms, helping them identify areas for AI implementation and develop a roadmap for successful adoption. Their approach is customized to each firm's unique needs, resources, and organizational culture.\n\nOther firms like RTS Labs and AI Smart Ventures also cater to mid-sized companies across various industries, focusing on practical AI guidance, automating routine tasks, and offering boutique approaches for faster time-to-value and lower costs. Similarly, MidMarket AI specifically helps mid-sized businesses adopt and implement AI tools to enhance performance and integrate solutions into existing operational systems. These consultants understand the need for flexible, cost-effective solutions that can be rapidly deployed and integrated without extensive disruption for small and mid-sized businesses."
                }
